            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Starstone sentries maintain the Starstone reactor and guard its approaches against intruders. Each Starstone sentry was created from a Starstone guardian and bears a magicircuitry pattern of that guardian, although the sentry's circuitry is neither an exact duplicate nor a perfect reflection. It's not clear what prompts Starstone guardians to create these sentries, or even what the process for creating them entails, but more Starstone sentries appear, glowing and new, before times of great danger to the Starstone or upheaval on Absalom Station.</p>\n<p>Slightly smaller and more fragile than their guardian progenitors, Starstone sentries are nevertheless just as diligent about protecting the Starstone-powered reactor at the heart of Absalom Station. Starstone sentries act and speak in unnerving symmetry, especially when they are close together. Despite having a superficial appearance that matches one specific guardian more than any others, every Starstone sentry unfailingly follows directions of any guardian.</p><h2>STARSTONE CONSTRUCTS</h2><p>Starstone constructs are ancient magitech constructs that serve to protect and maintain the Starstone reactor, the station's power source fueled by the legendary Starstone. They are reticent and standoffish creatures whose sole area of concern is the reactor and its continued functionality. Starstone constructs are vigilant and pious, performing their duties with unmistakable reverence. They are almost never seen outside of the Spike, and only rarely outside the chambers around the Starstone reactor. They attempt to complete whatever tasks take them away from their primary focus quickly and efficiently.</p>\n<p>Starstone constructs are tall, broad-shouldered robotic humanoids of gleaming platinum with slender limbs made of a translucent blue crystal. Their faces are mask-like and nearly featureless but for three circular eye holes containing luminous spheres that blink, widen, narrow, and otherwise move like a biological creature's eyes. Each Starstone construct has a pattern of intricate magicircuitry etched into their crystalline limbs and down the sides of their metallic torso.</p>\n<p>Starstone constructs have humanlike forms but don't follow most humanoid customs and habits, except for a custom of adorning themselves with cloth drapery, similar to how a humanoid would wear clothing. Starstone stoles are embroidered with spelled thread and are believed to contain immense magical energy.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Starfinder Absalom Station"
            }
        },
